<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36012" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phĭlēmo</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-on</span></b> , ŏnis, m.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φιλήμων</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A Greek comic poet</i>, <i>a native of
				Soli</i>, <i>in Cilicia</i>, <i>and
				a contemporary of Menander</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Trin. prol. 10</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Quint. 10,
				1, 72</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 17, 4, 1</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">App. Flor. 3, p.
			353</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An historian</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 13,
				27, § 95</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b> In mythology, <i>a pious
			rustic</i>, <i>the husband of Baucis</i>, Ov M. 8,
			631 sq.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
